Who all thinks that backed up save games is cheating?  I do it regularly
and without remorse.  I was raised on games such as Infocom's (where 
anything can kill you without warning) and Wizardry (where death is
frequent from masses of monsters) where saving and restoring was absolutely
necessary to finish the game.  I'm not talking about restoring the game
until you get the result you want (like redoing failed enchants to get a
+49 Mjollnir) but restoring if you get killed or totally stuck.  

I say that I have no remorse because (a) By the time I care enough to
dupe save files I've invested 10 hours or so in a character, (b) The
game can crash unexpectedly, at any time, rubbing out a character that
may have done nothing wrong, and (c) I don't see how its any different
from any other game that does have a save feature.

Is there anyone out there who finished any of the Ultima, King's Quest,
Wizardry, SSI AD&D, Infocom, whatever games WITHOUT falling back upon
a previously saved position?  

